om $\\text{L4}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by {{field-3}}."}] :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/math-academy-id 6690 :topic/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229146 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dr} =-\\frac{1.331 \\cdot 10^{14}}{r^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228256} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dr} =-\\frac{1.215 \\cdot 10^{14}}{r^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228257} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v\\frac{dv}{dr} =-\\frac{1.215 \\cdot 10^{14}}{r^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228258} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v\\frac{dv}{dr} =-\\frac{0.988 \\cdot 10^{14}}{r^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228259} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v\\frac{dv}{dr} =-\\frac{1.331 \\cdot 10^{14}}{r^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228260}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228255}] :question/math-academy-id "q-335225" :question/problem "Consider a spherical planet with radius $(5.5 \\cdot 10^{6})m$ and surface gravitational acceleration $g = 4.4m/s^{2}$. Which differential equation best models the velocity $v$ of an object projected radially outward from the planet, where $r$ is the distance from the planet's center to the object? Assume the only force acting on the object is the force due to gravity."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v\\frac{dv}{d